    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10973" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνωτερικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>upper</i> in point of place, <i>inland</i> (v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνω</span> (B) <i><span class="en">
				A.
				11.1f
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Act.Ap.</u>
				19.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of a
			medicine, <i>given by the mouth,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχίσκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archig.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				9.42
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cass.Fel.
				48
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span>”
				<i>medicine which takes effect upwards, emetic,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Superf.</u>
					29
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				10.969
			</span></i>.</div>
